68758943.markup:
(00:00:00) The Power of Threat Analytics (00:00:01) The Neglect of Threat Analytics (00:00:49) The True Potential of Threat Analytics (00:01:57) The Covenant: Read, Test, Act, Verify (00:04:55) The Three Oversights That Make Threat Analytics Ineffective (00:09:49) The Hour of Ordered Steps (00:16:46) Two Live Scenarios: Token Theft and Living Off the Land (00:23:14) Measurement and Governance: The Keys to Success (00:27:02) The Covenant in Action In {{link|https://www.m365.fm/unlocking-value-of-microsoft-365-threat-analytics/|this episode}} of M365.fm, Mirko Peters breaks open one of the most misunderstood {{link|https://www.m365.fm/categories/security-talk/|security}} capabilities in Microsoft 365: Threat Analytics — and shows how to turn it from a passive news feed into a weekly engine for real detections, closed attack paths, and measurable {{link|https://www.m365.fm/microsoft-secure-score-simply-explained/|Secure Score}} improvements. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- What Threat Analytics actually is: global intelligence, Microsoft IR experience, MITRE mapping, tenant exposure, and concrete recommendations in one place{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- The three oversights that make Threat Analytics look “useless”: skipping MITRE techniques, treating recommendations as optional, and ignoring device/account evidence{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- The One‑Hour Method: a repeatable workflow to go from report → hunting → incidents → Secure Score actions → verification in a single session{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to extract techniques, TTPs, and artifacts and turn them into targeted hunting queries in Microsoft 365 Defender{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to use Threat Analytics to uncover real detection gaps like OAuth abuse, token replay, and living‑off‑the‑land persistence{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to measure success with time‑to‑detect, attack paths closed, Secure Score controls implemented, and exposure trending{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT Threat Analytics isn’t useless — it’s unused. Most organizations scroll the headline, skip the MITRE mapping, and never bind recommendations to owners, SLAs, or Secure Score.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} Threat Analytics only becomes powerful when you treat each report as a mini playbook: read with intent, test with queries, act with controls, and verify with evidence. This episode argues that once you adopt a simple read → test → act → verify loop, Threat Analytics stops being a dashboard you scroll past and becomes the weekly engine that shortens dwell time and closes real attack paths in your tenant. WHY YOUR THREAT ANALYTICS IS FAILING YOU
- Reports are read like newsletters, not like incident reduction projects{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- MITRE techniques, artifacts, and exposure panels are ignored, so teams never see how “this is happening here”{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Recommendations are treated as suggestions instead of mapped to Secure Score, owners, and deadlines{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Device and account evidence is skipped, leaving real signals buried in telemetry{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE ONE‑HOUR METHOD (FIELD‑TESTED WORKFLOW) In about 60 minutes, your team can:
- Pick one relevant Threat Analytics report and extract techniques, TTPs, and artifacts{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Build focused hunting queries in Defender using those techniques and indicators{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Correlate hits to incidents and real assets in your tenant{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Assign Secure Score recommendations to named owners with SLAs{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Implement and verify controls, then rerun hunts to confirm the attack path is closed{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

WHY THIS EPISODE MATTERS
- You will see how Threat Analytics links incidents, telemetry, and Secure Score into one defensive narrative{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- You’ll learn how to close high‑value attack paths like phishing → OAuth consent abuse → token replay, and LOLBin‑based persistence using Threat Analytics as your guide{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- You’ll understand which metrics actually prove value: time‑to‑detect, techniques covered, controls implemented, and exposure reduced over time{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

WHO THIS EPISODE IS FOR This episode is essential for Microsoft 365 security engineers, SOC analysts, DFIR specialists, and cloud security architects responsible for defending Microsoft 365.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} If Threat Analytics in your tenant feels like a pretty but mostly ignored page, this conversation will give you a concrete way to turn it into a weekly habit that measurably reduces risk. ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 consultant and digital workplace architect focused on building attack‑aware, telemetry‑driven security programs on the Microsoft cloud.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68758943/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} Through M365.fm, Mirko shares practical workflows, governance patterns, and real‑world stories that help security teams turn Microsoft 365 features like Threat Analytics into repeatable, evidence‑based defense routines. Become a supporter of this podcast: {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/m365-fm-microsoft-365-azure-cloud-power-platform-ai--6704921/support?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss|https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/m365-fm-microsoft-365-azure-cloud-power-platform-ai--6704921/support}}.

68757235.markup:
(00:00:00) Zero Trust and Log Analysis (00:00:21) The Importance of Continuous Monitoring (00:00:37) Identity Verification: The First Line of Defense (00:01:26) Risky Sign-Ins: The Early Warning Sign (00:02:42) Combining Logs for Comprehensive Visibility (00:05:44) The Power of Lateral Movement Detection (00:07:51) Data Staging: The Next Stage of Attack (00:12:53) The Critical Role of Retention Policies (00:17:44) Copilot Interactions: A New Frontier in Detection (00:24:00) Case Study: A Quiet Data Exfiltration In this episode of M365.fm, Mirko Peters shows why Zero Trust without audit evidence is policy theater — and how to use Microsoft 365 audit logs to catch the quiet exfiltration and lateral movement your dashboards miss. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- Why a 12,000‑file SharePoint download in 20 minutes can pass every “green” Zero Trust check{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to fuse Entra ID sign‑in risk, Unified Audit Log events, Purview policy changes, and Copilot interactions into one coherent attack timeline{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- The difference between risky sign‑ins, risk detections, and workload identity anomalies — and why the retention gap matters{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to spot the three‑stream pattern that precedes most real data staging: risk, privilege change, and data surge{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to turn audit traces into KQL hunting queries, alerts, dashboards, and automation in Sentinel or Microsoft 365 Defender{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Practical techniques for building per‑user baselines so you can see the difference between sync and staging{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT Zero Trust is not what you configure; it’s what actually happens — and you only see that in logs. Conditional Access can “succeed” while an attacker quietly replays tokens, stages data, and widens sharing scopes.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} The real story starts when movement begins: inbox rules, mailbox forwarding, new sync relationships, sudden file surges, and “anyone” links — all stitched together by audit evidence.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} This episode argues that if you’re not joining Entra risk, Unified Audit Log events, Purview changes, and Copilot logs, you don’t have Zero Trust — you have a policy slide deck. WHY M365 AUDIT LOGS ARE YOUR REAL ZERO TRUST ENGINE
- Entra ID sign‑in & risk provide the prologue: risky sign‑ins, risk detections, and anomalous tokens before any data moves{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- The Unified Audit Log traces lateral movement across Exchange, SharePoint, OneDrive, and Teams in one place{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Purview audit and policy logs show when retention, labels, or DLP are quietly weakened before exfiltration{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Copilot interaction logs reveal how attackers or insiders might weaponize AI to discover sensitive documents faster{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Combined, these logs let you reconstruct “who did what, from where, with which privileges, to which data” — and build detections from that reality{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

PRACTICAL DETECTION PATTERNS YOU’LL HEAR
- Repeated medium‑risk sign‑ins from new ASNs/IPs followed by SharePoint download bursts{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Mailbox rule creation or forwarding changes paired with sudden OneDrive/SharePoint activity{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- New sync clients plus hundreds of unique files touched in a short time window{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- SharingLinkCreated events widening scope to “Anyone” or “Organization” right before or after file surges{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

WHO THIS EPISODE IS FOR This episode is essential for Microsoft 365 security engineers, incident responders, SOC analysts, and cloud architects responsible for Zero Trust and data protection in M365.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} If your tenant looks healthy in portals but you can’t explain how you’d spot a “clean” exfiltration case, this conversation will give you concrete queries, pivots, and patterns to fix that. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 consultant and digital workplace architect focused on building attack‑aware, evidence‑driven security programs on the Microsoft cloud.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68757235/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} Through M365.fm, Mirko shares practical investigations, KQL approaches, and governance patterns that help security teams turn Microsoft 365 audit logs into the backbone of real Zero Trust Explore more on M365.FM
- {{link|https://www.m365.fm/microsoft-365-audit-logs-zero-trust-essentials/|Full episode page with transcript, key takeaways and FAQ}}
- {{link|https://www.m365.fm/intune-deployment-security-risks-misconfigurations/|Harden Intune Deployment for Zero Trust Compliance}}
- {{link|https://www.m365.fm/global-secure-access-simply-explained/|Global Secure Access - Simply Explained}}
- {{link|https://www.m365.fm/categories/security-talk/|More Microsoft Security episodes on M365.FM}}
