68692737.markup:
(00:00:00) The Heresy of Manual Sharing (00:00:42) The Dangers of Scattered Truth (00:02:26) The Sanctuary of Org Apps (00:02:57) The Five Pillars of Governance (00:05:51) The Importance of Roles and Boundaries (00:09:57) The Lamp That Goes Out (00:14:19) The Canonical Doorway (00:20:35) The Procession of Deployment (00:24:27) The Thirty-Day Right of Migration (00:29:16) The Charge and Call to Action Govern Power BI reports with organizational apps, certified semantic models, deployment pipelines, RLS, labels, audiences, tenant rules, and clear ownership. In this episode of M365.fm, Mirko Peters lays out a governance doctrine for Power BI: why manual sharing is heresy, why reports need apostolic succession from dataset to Org App, and how to build a distribution pattern that keeps truth, lineage, and access under control. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- Why ad‑hoc share links, emailed PDFs, and private bookmarks quietly destroy lineage and trust in Power BI{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to make Org Apps the canonical doorway for consumers — and kill the “send me your version” culture{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to design RLS and OLS as guardianship, not guesswork: clear personas, stable roles, and tested audiences from Dev to Prod{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to stop stale workspaces and “Final_v7” reports from misleading leaders months after projects end{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to use deployment pipelines as your liturgy: Dev → Test → Prod with endorsements, labels, and tenant settings as the covenant{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to align sensitivity labels, tenant settings, and workspace strategy so classification and protection travel with your data{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT Most Power BI pain is not DAX — it is distribution. Every manual share breaks the chain between certified datasets, governed workspaces, and the Org App that should act as the single source of truth.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} When you treat Org Apps as the only doorway, RLS/OLS as sacred boundaries at the dataset, and deployment pipelines as your promotion ritual, you replace rumor dashboards with a canon of endorsed, testable truth. This episode argues that Power BI governance is less about adding tools and more about removing alternate paths — so if it’s not in the app, it’s not trusted, and if it bypasses lineage, it doesn’t get used. WHO THIS EPISODE IS FOR This episode is essential for Power BI admins, data architects, BI leads, and analytics product owners responsible for enterprise reporting on Microsoft Fabric and Power BI.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} If your organization is drowning in conflicting dashboards, stale workspaces, and shadow copies of “the truth,” this conversation will give you a concrete doctrine for report distribution, RLS/OLS, and workspace strategy that users and leadership can actually live with. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 and data platform consultant who helps organizations turn Power BI and Microsoft Fabric into governed, trustworthy analytics platforms.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} Through M365.fm, Mirko shares practical governance patterns, workspace strategies, and real‑world stories that help teams move from scattered reports to a disciplined Power BI distribution model.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68692737/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} Explore more on M365.FM
