(00:00:00) The Copilot Training Dilemma (00:00:30) The Limitations of Traditional Training (00:01:50) The Shadow Training Economy (00:02:42) Building an Evergreen Copilot Learning Center (00:03:38) The Architecture of the Copilot Hub (00:04:58) Implementing Governance and Search (00:10:19) Safety Scaffolding and Feedback Loops (00:11:14) Case Study: Enterprise Adoption Success (00:14:21) The Governance Switch to Kill Shadow Training (00:17:50) Measuring Success and Key Takeaways Build a governed Copilot Learning Center with role-based guidance, tenant-aware content, ownership, review cycles, analytics, and a trusted source for adoption. In this episode of M365.fm, Mirko Peters shows why most Copilot rollouts drown in random decks, “ultimate prompt guides,” and ad‑hoc Teams channels — and how a single governed Copilot Learning Center can replace that chaos with one trusted hub for every user. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- Why classic Copilot training (one‑off webinars, PDFs, random links) always decays into confusion and shadow content{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to design a Copilot Learning Center as a real product: clear owners, roadmap, KPIs, and a backlog{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to structure the hub into three zones — Learn, Do, Govern — so users always know where to go{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to build an opinionated prompt library that focuses on intent, anatomy, and failure modes, not just examples{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to connect Copilot guidance to real roles (HR, finance, sales, IT) instead of generic “top 10 prompts”{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to stop shadow training: freshness badges, redirects, and “not authoritative” labels for legacy content{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Which metrics actually prove value: ticket deflection, search success, prompt reuse, and return visits{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT Copilot success is not about one big training; it is about a system that users can trust every day. When guidance is scattered across wikis, PDFs, Teams chats, and vendor decks, nobody knows what is current, what is allowed, or which Copilot to use — and your help desk pays the price. A Copilot Learning Center treats adoption like a product: one front door, curated content, clear governance, and measurable outcomes. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHO THIS EPISODE IS FOR This episode is ideal for digital workplace leaders, adoption and change managers, Copilot program owners, and IT teams who are accountable for Copilot success — not just license deployment. If your users keep asking the same Copilot questions in different places, this conversation gives you a concrete blueprint for one governed hub that finally answers them. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 consultant and digital workplace architect focused on building governed, evergreen adoption systems for Microsoft Copilot and modern work. Through M365.fm, Mirko shares practical architectures, governance patterns, and KPI playbooks that help organizations replace chaotic training efforts with durable learning centers that actually reduce tickets and increase safe, effective Copilot usage.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68604476/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} Explore more on M365.FM
