68519897.markup:
(00:00:00) The Slow Cloud Drive Dilemma (00:00:38) The Old Sync Method: A Legacy Approach (00:00:59) The Hidden Costs of Full Sync (00:03:36) The Benefits of OneDrive Shortcuts (00:08:15) Step-by-Step Guide to Adding Shortcuts (00:10:48) Common Mistakes to Avoid with Shortcuts (00:11:39) Organizing and Maintaining Shortcuts Effectively (00:15:32) The Decision Matrix for Sync vs. Shortcuts (00:18:36) Future-Proofing Your Cloud Storage Replace OneDrive library sync with shortcuts to reduce duplicate files, sync conflicts, CPU load, storage use, bandwidth waste, and broken versions. In this episode of M365.fm, Mirko Peters explains why “sync the whole SharePoint library” is a 2007 habit that kills device performance, breaks governance, and makes every new laptop feel slow — and how OneDrive shortcuts give you a cloud‑native way to work only where it matters. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- The hidden costs of full‑library sync: metadata overhead, file system tax, network churn, storage creep, and a much larger failure surface{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How local copies quietly undermine governance by enabling forks outside SharePoint retention, sensitivity labels, and versioning{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How OneDrive shortcuts create lightweight “doors” to the exact folders you use, roaming with your account across devices{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- A step‑by‑step playbook to replace legacy syncs with targeted shortcuts and selective offline files{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Naming and organization patterns so your shortcuts behave like a clean hallway of work hubs instead of a second junk drawer{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- A simple decision matrix: when to use shortcuts, when constrained full sync still makes sense, and when a simple share link is enough{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT Full‑library sync optimizes for emotional comfort, not efficiency. Modern OneDrive is built for “visibility without possession”: shortcuts keep you in the governed SharePoint source while shrinking your sync graph, reducing conflicts, and making machines feel fast again. If you treat OneDrive like a cloud OS for doors instead of a copy machine, your storage, bandwidth, and audit logs all improve. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHO THIS EPISODE IS FOR This episode is ideal for Microsoft 365 admins, digital workplace owners, and power users who constantly troubleshoot sync errors, slow laptops, and “Where is the latest version?” drama. If your environment is full of giant synced libraries and confused users, this conversation gives you both the narrative and the concrete steps to roll out shortcuts as the new default.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519897/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 consultant focused on modern work, governance, and performance‑friendly collaboration architectures. Through M365.fm, Mirko turns abstract M365 features into practical habits and rollout kits so organizations can get the benefits of the cloud without living in sync hell. Explore more on M365.FM
- {{link|https://www.m365.fm/stop-syncing-onedrive-use-shortcuts/|Full episode page with transcript, key takeaways and FAQ}}
