68519435.markup:
(00:00:00) The Cloud's Hidden Costs (00:01:13) The Illusion of Cloud Computing (00:01:43) Azure ARC: The Universal Remote Control (00:04:29) The MINIPC Revolution (00:07:35) Identity Crisis: Overcoming the AD Trap (00:11:51) Deploying Your Own Azure Region (00:16:32) The Economics of Cloud at Home (00:21:46) The Cloud Domesticated Cut Azure costs with Azure Arc and Azure Local on mini PCs while keeping Policy, Defender, RBAC, monitoring, Key Vault identity, VMs, and AKS under governance. In this episode of M365.fm, Mirko Peters shows how to keep Azure’s control plane while you stop renting generic cloud VMs, by running Azure Local on small, Arc-managed mini PCs that behave like your own private region on a desk or at the edge. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- How Azure Arc “badges” on-prem servers so Policy, Defender, Monitor, and RBAC apply from the same Azure portal.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How Azure Local brings core Azure services (VMs, AKS, networking) to those Arc-managed mini PCs for near-zero-latency workloads.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Why modern mini PCs (i5/i7 or Ryzen, 32–64 GB RAM, NVMe) are enough to host serious edge or branch workloads.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How zero-touch enrollment works with voucher USBs so non-experts can plug in hardware that auto-joins Azure and applies baseline policy.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Why you should skip a full AD forest and use certificate-based identity with Key Vault for clean, auditable zero-trust at the edge.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to deploy VMs and AKS with the same wizards and GitOps flows you already use in public Azure.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- The real economics: Arc registration is free, you mainly pay for governance and observability services instead of per-hour VM meters.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT You can keep Azure’s brain (governance, security, portal) while owning the hardware muscle that runs your workloads. Azure Arc plus Azure Local turns mini PCs into tiny Azure regions, with the same policies, Defender rules, RBAC, and audit trails you rely on in the cloud — but with predictable capex instead of surprise VM bills. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHO THIS EPISODE IS FOR This episode is ideal for CIOs and CFOs cutting cloud spend, platform teams standardizing hybrid control, DevOps/SREs chasing latency-sensitive workloads, and edge-heavy industries like retail, manufacturing, and healthcare. If you are paying for 24×7 cloud VMs that rarely burst, this conversation gives you a concrete architecture and checklist to bring those workloads home without losing Azure governance. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 and Azure consultant focused on secure, governed hybrid architectures that mix cloud control with local performance. Through M365.fm, Mirko shares practical patterns for Azure Arc, Azure Local, GitOps, and cost control so teams can build edge fleets that feel like Azure regions, not snowflake servers under someone’s desk.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519435/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} Explore more on M365.FM
- {{link|https://www.m365.fm/azure-arc-azure-local-mini-pc-cloud-alternative/|Full episode page with transcript, key takeaways and FAQ}}
- {{link|https://www.m365.fm/stop-paying-for-nothing/|Build an Automated Azure Cleanup Engine to Reduce Cloud Waste}}
