68519015.markup:
(00:00:00) The Evolution of AI Interaction (00:00:52) The Typing Bottleneck (00:03:30) Voice Intelligence: The Next Frontier (00:06:51) The RAG Pattern: Retrieval-Augmented Generation (00:12:08) Secure and Governed Voice Interaction (00:17:19) Deploying Voice-Driven Knowledge (00:21:46) The Future of AI Interaction In this episode of M365.fm, Mirko Peters shows how to break the “40 words per minute” bottleneck by giving Copilot a real-time voice, backed by GPT‑4o Realtime and Azure AI Search, so you can talk to your company’s knowledge layer instead of typing at it. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- Why keyboards throttle copilots designed for millisecond reasoning, and how voice restores natural flow in meetings and deep work.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How GPT‑4o Realtime turns Copilot into a full duplex assistant with low-latency audio, barge‑in, and human‑like turn taking.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How Azure AI Search plus RAG ground every spoken answer in governed company content, with citations and RBAC‑aware retrieval.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How a secure proxy layer keeps keys, tool calls, and policies in Azure instead of front-end apps.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to wire the mic in Teams, Copilot Studio, or Power Apps to a voice-enabled knowledge layer without breaking DLP, Purview, or audit.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- A concrete implementation checklist: data prep, indexing, proxy design, voice UX, security, and cost controls.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT Voice removes the human I/O bottleneck, GPT‑4o Realtime removes the latency, and Azure AI Search removes most hallucination. The real magic is not a fancy UI but a hardened proxy that orchestrates RAG, enforces scope and policy, and logs every call, so “talking to Copilot” is as compliant and auditable as sending an email. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHO THIS EPISODE IS FOR This episode is ideal for M365 architects, platform and AI teams, and business leaders who want Copilot to be genuinely conversational without sacrificing governance. If you’ve ever wished you could just talk through a problem with Copilot during a live meeting and get cited answers in real time, this conversation gives you the architecture to make that safe and real. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68519015/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 consultant focused on building governed, voice‑enabled productivity experiences on Azure and M365. Through M365.fm, Mirko shares practical blueprints for Copilot, RAG, and voice integration so organizations can add a microphone to their knowledge layer without adding a new risk category. Become a supporter of this podcast: {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/m365-fm-microsoft-365-azure-cloud-power-platform-ai--6704921/support?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss|https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/m365-fm-microsoft-365-azure-cloud-power-platform-ai--6704921/support}}.

68518731.markup:
(00:00:00) The Cloud Migration Trap (00:00:16) The Illusion of Cloud First (00:01:20) The AI-Hostile Legacy of Lift and Shift (00:04:00) Data Readiness: The Foundation of AI (00:07:47) Infrastructure and MLOps Maturity (00:11:20) The Talent and Governance Gap (00:14:27) A Cautionary Tale: Fintracks' AI Journey (00:17:04) The Three-Step AI-Ready Cloud Strategy (00:21:26) The Path to AI Inevitability Make cloud migration AI-ready by replacing lift-and-shift debt with unified data, MLOps maturity, governance, secure permissions, lineage, and cost discipline. In this episode of M365.fm, Mirko Peters argues that “cloud-first” is not the same as “AI-ready” — and that lift‑and‑shift migrations often preserve exactly the chaos that makes Copilots dangerous, expensive, and hard to govern. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHAT YOU WILL LEARN
- Why VMs in Azure don’t buy you structure, lineage, or identity discipline — they just rehost sprawl in someone else’s data center{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How lift‑and‑shift keeps legacy directory trees, broken tagging, and permission sprawl that suffocate AI projects{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- The three pillars of AI readiness: data readiness (structure + lineage), infrastructure & MLOps maturity, and talent & governance competence{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How Fabric and Purview work together to unify analytics, enforce classification, and give you traceable data pipelines end‑to‑end{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How Azure AI Foundry, Azure ML, and governance‑as‑code (Policy, Bicep, Blueprints) turn models and datasets into controlled, repeatable assets{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Why you must convert traditional roles (DBAs, network, compliance) into data custodians, identity stewards, and AI risk auditors{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- A three‑step strategy: Unify your data estate, Fortify with governance‑as‑code, and Automate intelligence feedback loops{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT Cloud ≠ AI. Without structure, lineage, and identity discipline, you are just modernizing chaos and giving Copilots a bigger blast radius. AI‑ready means you can prove where critical data came from, who touched it, how models used it, and how you would roll back if something goes wrong — in minutes, not months. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHO THIS EPISODE IS FOR This episode is ideal for CIOs, CDOs, heads of AI, enterprise architects, and compliance leaders who are being told “we’re cloud‑first, so we’re ready for AI” but suspect the foundation is brittle. If your roadmap still looks like a relocation project instead of an AI architecture, this conversation gives you a concrete checklist to course‑correct before Copilots hit production. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68518731/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}ABOUT THE HOST Mirko Peters is a Microsoft 365 and cloud governance consultant focused on building AI‑ready data estates on Microsoft Fabric and Azure. Through M365.fm, Mirko shares practical patterns, governance‑as‑code templates, and real‑world stories that help organizations move from “percent of servers migrated” to “percent of decisions that are traceable and defensible. Explore more on M365.FM
