- What Forrester’s Total Economic Impact model says about Copilot ROI and payback.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Where the hidden cost of routine work sits in calendars, inboxes and reports.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How small improvements in opportunity volume and win rates translate into revenue.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Why data quality, governance and adoption are critical to real Copilot impact.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to think about “nine hours saved per user per month” in practical terms.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Concrete examples of Copilot impact in go‑to‑market, operations and people & culture.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to test Copilot value by role with simple, recurring use cases.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

THE CORE INSIGHT The core insight of this episode is that the real cost you’re paying today isn’t the Copilot license fee – it’s the massive, mostly invisible drag of routine work that looks busy but creates little value. By combining Microsoft 365 Copilot with solid data readiness and intentional usage patterns, you don’t just free hours, you change how those hours are invested in revenue, innovation and retention, making the case for Copilot as a tool that can genuinely pay for itself. {{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/68135055/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}WHO THIS IS FOR
