- How embedding Dynamics 365 Sales into Teams channels and meetings turns CRM data into live context—not static screenshots.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67357747/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67357747/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to design role‑specific views in Teams so each sales persona sees the data that actually matters to them.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67357747/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67357747/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How Power Automate and adaptive cards turn routine updates and approvals into quick actions inside chat.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67357747/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67357747/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How to keep Dynamics 365 as the single source of truth while making Teams the primary home for day‑to‑day sales work.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67357747/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67357747/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

