67323819.markup:
If you’ve ever shipped a Power App and hoped users wouldn’t trip over hidden bugs, {{link|https://www.m365.fm/automated-testing-for-power-apps-and-dataverse/|this episode}} is for you. We start with the myth that “low‑code apps don’t need automated testing” and show how that belief quietly puts your business data, compliance, and downstream systems at risk. Using real incidents—from broken money fields to silent data loss during Dataverse migrations—we unpack how small, untested changes in “simple” apps turn into expensive reconciliation projects, audit headaches, and late‑night firefights.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} We then dive into the hidden complexity under the drag‑and‑drop surface. You’ll hear how {{link|https://www.m365.fm/power-apps-simply-explained/|Power Apps}} sit on top of Dataverse logic, security roles, environment variables, and ever‑changing connectors, which means each tweak to schemas, permissions, or flows can ripple across Teams, Outlook, and Power BI without obvious errors. We explore scenarios like vacation request apps that accidentally expose HR data, environment variable changes that silently point apps at the wrong data source, and conditional formulas that behave differently for each role—problems no quick UAT walkthrough will ever fully catch.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}} From there, we look at why manual testing alone can’t keep up as apps and environments evolve. Real users don’t live on the “happy path”: licenses expire, connectors change behavior, fields start allowing nulls, and integrations drift over time. You’ll learn why relying on ad‑hoc business testing is like checking a car’s paint but never its brakes, and how automated tests—covering critical flows, permissions, and data rules—become essential once Power Apps handle invoices, approvals, customer data, or compliance‑relevant records. By the end, you’ll see automated testing not as overkill for low‑code, but as the only realistic way to keep up with the pace and reach of your apps. You’ll walk away with a clearer mental model: treat every Power App as part of a larger system, assume every schema or connector change can break something unseen, and use automated tests to catch those failures before your accounting team, auditors, or customers do. WHAT YOU LEARN
- Why “it’s just a Power App” is one of the costliest myths in modern IT.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How small schema and connector changes in Dataverse and Power Apps can cause silent data corruption and loss.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Why manual “happy path” testing by business users misses the most dangerous edge cases.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- How hidden complexity (roles, environment variables, connectors, downstream systems) multiplies risk over time.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}
- Why automated testing is becoming essential infrastructure for serious {{link|https://www.m365.fm/power-platform-simply-explained/|Power Platform}} workloads.{{link|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266|https://www.spreaker.com/cms/episodes/67323819/edit/info?filter=NETWORK&network=18613266}}

